Read an empty Vorbis comment as absent, so it no longer blocks tag writes.

Why: the tag writer refused any FLAC/Ogg/Opus file holding one empty comment
(`LYRICS=`, `BAND=`), because lofty drops empties on save. Library Management
then blocks the file and, through it, its whole album: the activation dry run
of 2026-10-24 blocked 38 files with "The file's LYRICS/BAND tag is empty" and
87 more as BUNDLE_BLOCKED. An empty comment carries no value, so the Vorbis
parser now leaves it out: reads see the field as absent, a save drops the key,
its verify compares the tag without it, and an undo replays a document that
never held it (a replay of "" would itself be refused as not expressible).

Tests: the two upstream tests that pinned the refusal now pin the drop (the
fixture with empty TITLE/ARTIST/ALBUM saves; an injected empty comment goes,
every other comment stays, and a replay of the read document saves). Both fail
without the source change. Full `cargo test --test library` and
`-p droppedneedle-library --lib` on macOS: identical failure set with and
without the patch (72 + 4, pre-existing, platform).

Remove when: upstream stops refusing empty Vorbis comments.

